{
  "corpusSha": "7aaf6bf35ca117adf0a57522e4db87b7f1b5ab00",
  "rationales": {
    "decision-recorded-as-a-flag": "A checkpoint option writes the decision it recorded into a flag, and no gate, loop or transition tests it. The decision itself is durable in the session checkpoint response, so the flag adds a second record of the same fact rather than state a run consumes.",
    "phase-marker-with-no-branch": "A step marks its own phase complete on a path that has no branch to gate. The value is honest and no route asks for it, so it is state a variant would need rather than state this graph reads.",
    "iteration-item-outlives-its-loop": "A loop binds its item variable and the body reads it by field rather than by name, so the declared name has no reader of its own.",
    "output-unconsumed-at-the-activity-seam": "The bound operation lands an output in the bag and nothing downstream reads it. The technique-layer view of the same seam is the binding-fidelity dead-output finding, where it is triaged against the file that declares it."
  },
